From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dariusz Majnert <dariusz.majnert@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 16:58:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] emc: own transactional tool CRUD in task

Ported to v2.10.0-pre2. Task reads the changer's HAL pins through
upstream's hal_get_bool()/hal_get_si32(). The read-only mmap remapping
uses upstream's mmap_is_creator and mmap_fd (8c8e048) instead of its own
creator flag and closed descriptor; a replaced or vanished mapping also
closes its descriptor.

Kept from the tool wear patch: a tool line is at most 510 characters,
and a table whose line is too long is not written (the temporary file is
dropped, so the table file stays as it was) and the edit is not
published. A table loaded with lines refused as too long is not saved
over until a table without them is loaded; tooldata_load_snapshot()
reports refused lines and the caller records them when it publishes the
table. G10 tool edits whose save fails are still rolled back.
tooldata_save() keeps upstream's message for a missing [EMCIO]TOOL_TABLE.

Upstream's G10 db_program notification (b53e523) stays in place but is a
no-op, since IO initialization now refuses [EMCIO]DB_PROGRAM; the
tests/tooldb tests, which need a db program, are skipped.
